{"id":"s3.1.1","slug":"gcd-and-lcm","title":"GCD and LCM","content":"<p class=\"mb-4\">Finding the Greatest Common Divisor (GCD) and Least Common Multiple (LCM) is a common task.</p><p class=\"mb-4\"><strong>GCD via Euclid's Algorithm:</strong> To find GCD(a, b) with $a < b$, find the remainder when $b$ is divided by $a$, let's call it $r_1$. Now, GCD(a, b) = GCD($r_1$, a). Repeat this process until the remainder is 0. The last non-zero remainder is the GCD. For example, GCD(36, 60) $\\rightarrow$ GCD(24, 36) $\\rightarrow$ GCD(12, 24) = 12.</p><p class=\"mb-4\"><strong>LCM Formula:</strong> Once the GCD is known, the LCM can be found easily using the formula: $LCM(a, b) = \\frac{a \\times b}{GCD(a, b)}$.</p><p>For example, $LCM(36, 60) = \\frac{36 \\times 60}{12} = 3 \\times 60 = 180$.</p>","summary":"Finding the Greatest Common Divisor (GCD) and Least Common Multiple (LCM) is a common task.","generation_guideline":"Ask for the GCD or LCM of two 2-digit numbers.","questions":[{"id":1,"text":"The GCF of 35 and 63 is:","answer":"7","kind":"exact","tags":["divisors"]},{"id":2,"text":"The LCM of 64 and 20 is:","answer":"320","kind":"exact","tags":["divisors"]},{"id":3,"text":"The LCM of 27 and 36 is:","answer":"108","kind":"exact","tags":["divisors"]},{"id":4,"text":"The GCF of 48 and 72 is:","answer":"24","kind":"exact","tags":["divisors"]},{"id":5,"text":"The GCD of 27 and 36 is:","answer":"9","kind":"exact","tags":["divisors"]},{"id":6,"text":"The LCM of 63 and 45 is:","answer":"315","kind":"exact","tags":["divisors"]},{"id":7,"text":"The GCD of 132 and 156 is:","answer":"12","kind":"exact","tags":["divisors"]},{"id":8,"text":"The LCM of 57 and 95 is:","answer":"285","kind":"exact","tags":["divisors"]},{"id":9,"text":"The GCD of 52 and 91 is:","answer":"13","kind":"exact","tags":["divisors"]},{"id":10,"text":"The LCM of 52 and 28 is:","answer":"364","kind":"exact","tags":["divisors"]},{"id":11,"text":"The GCD of 48 and 54 is:","answer":"6","kind":"exact","tags":["divisors"]},{"id":12,"text":"The GCD of 54 and 36 is:","answer":"18","kind":"exact","tags":["divisors"]},{"id":13,"text":"The LCM of 108 and 81 is:","answer":"324","kind":"exact","tags":["divisors"]},{"id":14,"text":"The GCD of 28 and 52 is:","answer":"4","kind":"exact","tags":["divisors"]},{"id":15,"text":"The LCM of 51 and 34 is:","answer":"102","kind":"exact","tags":["divisors"]},{"id":16,"text":"The LCM of $2^3 \\times 3^2$ and $2^2 \\times 3^3$ is:","answer":"216","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic","divisors"]},{"id":17,"text":"The LCM of 28 and 42 is:","answer":"84","kind":"exact","tags":["divisors"]},{"id":18,"text":"The LCM of 54 and 48 is:","answer":"432","kind":"exact","tags":["divisors"]},{"id":19,"text":"The LCM of 84 and 70 is:","answer":"420","kind":"exact","tags":["divisors"]},{"id":20,"text":"The GCF of 132 and 187 is:","answer":"11","kind":"exact","tags":["divisors"]},{"id":21,"text":"The LCM of 48 and 72 is:","answer":"144","kind":"exact","tags":["divisors"]},{"id":22,"text":"The GCF of 51, 68, and 85 is:","answer":"17","kind":"exact","tags":["divisors"]},{"id":23,"text":"The GCF(24, 44) − LCM(24, 44) =","answer":"-260","kind":"exact","tags":["divisors"]},{"id":24,"text":"The LCM of 16, 20, and 32 is:","answer":"160","kind":"exact","tags":["divisors"]},{"id":25,"text":"The GCD(15, 28) times LCM(15, 28) is:","answer":"420","kind":"exact","tags":["divisors"]},{"id":26,"text":"The LCM of 12, 18, and 20 is:","answer":"180","kind":"exact","tags":["divisors"]},{"id":27,"text":"The LCM of 14, 21, and 42 is:","answer":"42","kind":"exact","tags":["divisors"]},{"id":28,"text":"The LCM of 8, 18, and 32 is:","answer":"288","kind":"exact","tags":["divisors"]},{"id":29,"text":"The GCD(15, 21) + LCM(15, 21) =","answer":"108","kind":"exact","tags":["divisors"]},{"id":30,"text":"The GCF of 44, 66, and 88 is:","answer":"22","kind":"exact","tags":["divisors"]},{"id":31,"text":"The product of the GCF and LCM of 21 and 33 is:","answer":"693","kind":"exact","tags":["arit